config BR2_PACKAGE_QCOM_DSP_FIRMWARE
	bool "qcom-dsp-firmware"
	depends on BR2_aarch64
	help
	  Kernel-loaded Hexagon DSP firmware images (cdsp.mbn, adsp.mbn) for
	  the Radxa Dragon Q6A, installed under /lib/firmware/qcom at the
	  paths the DTB's remoteproc `firmware-name` properties point to:

	    remoteproc_cdsp: qcom/qcs6490/cdsp.mbn
	    remoteproc_adsp: qcom/qcs6490/radxa/dragon-q6a/adsp.mbn

	  These signed blobs are NOT in any public package or in
	  hexagon-dsp-binaries. They must be harvested from a stock RadxaOS
	  install (Phase 0) and dropped into
	  blobs/qcom-dsp-firmware/lib/firmware/... in this repo.

	  If the blobs are absent the package installs nothing (the build
	  still succeeds, e.g. for the QEMU smoke test), but the CDSP will
	  NOT come up on real hardware until they are provided. See
	  blobs/qcom-dsp-firmware/README.md.
